module

public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Geometric.SpecialFibreFirstOrder

/-!
# A generator of the defining ideal of the special fibre of a first-order deformation

Let `P` be a deformation of a scheme `X` over an object `A` of `𝒞_Λ`. The defining ideal of the
special-fibre immersion `P.specialMap` is the ideal sheaf `𝔪_A 𝒪` generated by the maximal ideal
of `A` (`Deformation.Examples.ker_eq_baseIdeal_of_isPullback`), so over an affine open it is the
image of `𝔪_A` under the structure map. When `𝔪_A` is **principal** — which for the dual numbers
`k[ε]` it is, generated by `ε` — the ideal over an affine open is therefore generated by the
single function that `ε` determines there.

That is the hypothesis `hgen` of
`Stacks.Thickenings.appLE_eq_mul_of_affineOpens_ker_eq_span`: generation of the defining ideal by
one function, affine-locally, which is all an `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData` ever
supplies. This file produces it for a first-order deformation, with the generator exhibited as the
restriction of a single *global* function on the total space, so that the restriction appearing in
`hgen` is again a generator over the smaller open.

## Main definitions

* `Deformation.Examples.baseSection`: the function on an open of a scheme over `Spec A`
  determined by an element of `A`.

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_dualNumberRingEquiv`: the maximal ideal of a local
  ring isomorphic to the dual numbers is generated by the preimage of `ε`.
* `Deformation.Examples.baseSection_map`: restricting the function determined by an element of
  the base gives the function determined by that same element.
* `Deformation.Examples.ker_app_specialMap_eq_span`: **the defining ideal of the special fibre
  over an affine open is generated by the function determined by a generator of the maximal ideal
  of the base.**

## Implementation notes

The generator of the maximal ideal is carried as a hypothesis `𝔪_A = (t)` on an element `t` of
the base rather than built from a coordinate, exactly as the square-zero hypothesis is carried in
`StacksFrontier/Deformation/Examples/Geometric/SpecialFibreFirstOrder.lean`: the two uses of the
generator — writing the ideal over an affine open and computing what a self-map does to it — want
the *same* element, and a hypothesis is the only way to share it. The hypothesis is discharged at
the dual-number object by `Deformation.Examples.maximalIdeal_artinianDualNumbers_eq_span`.

`Deformation.Examples.baseSection` is the restriction of
`Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseScalarMap`, the global function the base ring determines; it is
spelled as a restriction rather than as `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.appLE` of the structure map
so that `Deformation.Examples.baseSection_map` is one composition of restrictions.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DY7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DY7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CK2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CK2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

universe u

namespace Deformation.Examples

variable {Λ k : Type u} [CommRing Λ] [Field k] [Algebra Λ k]

/-! ### A generator of the maximal ideal of the base -/

/-- **A local ring isomorphic to the dual numbers has principal maximal ideal**, generated by the
preimage of `ε`. The maximal ideal of `k[ε]` is `(ε)` by
`DualNumber.maximalIdeal_eq_span_singleton_eps`, and an isomorphism of rings carries the maximal
ideal to the maximal ideal (`IsLocalRing.map_ringEquiv_maximalIdeal`) and a principal ideal to the
principal ideal on the image of the generator.

Only the ring structure enters, so the hypothesis is a ring isomorphism rather than an
isomorphism of `Λ`-algebras; that is what lets the statement be used both for an object of `𝒞_Λ`
and for the carrier of an object of a category of algebras over one of them. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_dualNumberRingEquiv {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    (e : A ≃+* DualNumber k) :
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A = Ideal.span {e.symm (DualNumber.eps (R := k))} := by
  rw [← IsLocalRing.map_ringEquiv_maximalIdeal e.symm,
    DualNumber.maximalIdeal_eq_span_singleton_eps, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]

/-- **The maximal ideal of the dual-number object of `𝒞_Λ` is principal**, the coordinate
hypothesis of `Deformation.Examples.maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_dualNumberRingEquiv` being discharged
by `Deformation.Examples.artinianDualNumbersCoordinate`. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_artinianDualNumbers_eq_span :
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal
        ((Deformation.artinianDualNumbers.{u, u, u} Λ k : ArtinianLocalAlgCat.{u, u, u} Λ k) :
          Type u) =
      Ideal.span {artinianDualNumbersCoordinate.toRingEquiv.symm (DualNumber.eps (R := k))} :=
  maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_dualNumberRingEquiv artinianDualNumbersCoordinate.toRingEquiv

/-! ### The function on a scheme over an affine base determined by an element of the base -/

/-- The function on an open of a scheme over `Spec A` determined by an element of `A`: the global
function `Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseScalarMap` of the structure morphism, restricted to the
open. -/
def baseSection {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {W : Scheme.{u}}
    (q : W ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) (t : A) (V : W.Opens) : Γ(W, V) :=
  (W.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V))).op).hom
    (Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseScalarMap q t)

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {W : Scheme.{u}} (q : W ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of A))

/-- **Restricting the function determined by an element of the base gives the function determined
by that same element**, both being restrictions of one global function. -/
theorem baseSection_map (t : A) {V V' : W.Opens} (hV : V' ≤ V) :
    (W.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op).hom (baseSection q t V) = baseSection q t V' := by
  rw [baseSection, baseSection, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- **The function determined by an element of the base is the restriction of the global function
`Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseScalarMap` determines**, which is the definition, stated for
rewriting. -/
theorem baseSection_eq_map_baseScalarMap (t : A) (V : W.Opens) :
    baseSection q t V = (W.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V))).op).hom
      (Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseScalarMap q t) :=
  rfl

/-- **The function determined by a product is the product of the functions**, both
`Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseScalarMap` and restriction being ring homomorphisms. -/
theorem baseSection_mul (a b : A) (V : W.Opens) :
    baseSection q a V * baseSection q b V = baseSection q (a * b) V := by
  rw [baseSection, baseSection, baseSection, ← map_mul, ← map_mul]

/-- **The function determined by an element of the base is the image of that element under the
comorphism of the structure morphism.** This is the form in which it meets
`Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseIdeal_ideal`. -/
theorem baseSection_eq_appLE (t : A) (V : W.Opens) :
    baseSection q t V =
      (q.appLE ⊤ V le_top).hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv.hom t) :=
  rfl

/-! ### The defining ideal over an affine open -/

variable {X : Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of k))}

/-- **The defining ideal of the special fibre over an affine open is generated by the function
determined by a generator of the maximal ideal of the base.** The ideal sheaf of the
special-fibre immersion is `𝔪_A 𝒪` (`Deformation.Examples.ker_eq_baseIdeal_of_isPullback`), whose
ideal over an affine open is the image of `𝔪_A` under the comorphism of the structure morphism
(`Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseIdeal_ideal`); the image of a principal ideal is principal on the
image of the generator.

This is the hypothesis `hgen` of
`Stacks.Thickenings.appLE_eq_mul_of_affineOpens_ker_eq_span`, with the generator exhibited as a
restriction of one global function so that `Deformation.Examples.baseSection_map` supplies the
restricted form the hypothesis asks for. -/
theorem ker_app_specialMap_eq_span (P : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) X)
    {t : (P.base : Type u)}
    (ht : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (P.base : Type u) = Ideal.span {t})
    (V : P.scheme.affineOpens) :
    RingHom.ker (P.specialMap.app V.1).hom = Ideal.span {baseSection P.toBase t V.1} := by
  have := deformationSpecialMap_isClosedImmersion P
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.ker_apply, ker_eq_baseIdeal_of_isPullback P.toBase P.specialCartesian,
    Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseIdeal_ideal, ht, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  rfl

end Deformation.Examples

end
